    "result_text": "Full suite is green. The build only has the one acceptance test class active, and it passes along with everything compiling.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `POST /api/owners` (and the `GET` read-back the test uses) to return a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo small, low-impact changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: no new method in the large `Owner` entity, no change to any OfficeFloor function class. The value is computed in the mapper \u2014 a small class with low surrounding complexity \u2014 from the stored names, so both the created and fetched owner return `\"LastName, FirstName\"`.",
